{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Range","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Inverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":53,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.mesonMassRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.mesonMassRatio","kind":"def","line":480,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L480-L485","doc":"The kaon–pion mass ratio `m_K/m_π = (q⁵ − q⁻⁵) · (9/5)²` from Hecke characters\nand Seifert volumes (`(q⁵−q⁻⁵) = χ_{(2,1)}(σ₁⁵)` on `T(2,5)`; `(9/5)²` the squared\nSeifert-volume ratio; power 2 = the two quarks of a meson). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.h_eq_qplus1_hbar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.h_eq_qplus1_hbar","kind":"theorem","line":474,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L474-L478","doc":"`h = (q+1)·ℏ` — the exact relation between `h = q − q⁻¹` and `ℏ = (q−1)/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.spectralCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.spectralCorrection","kind":"def","line":466,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L466-L472","doc":"The spectral correction factor for the proton mass,\n`arccos(1 − 3h⁴/2 − h⁶/2) / (8ℏ²)` with `h = q − q⁻¹`, `ℏ = (q−1)/q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.hecke_character_diag_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.hecke_character_diag_odd","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L434-L441","doc":"Scalar core of the standard-rep Hecke character at odd powers. On the Hoefsmit\ndiagonal basis `σ₁ = diag(q, −q⁻¹)`, `tr(σ₁ⁿ) = qⁿ + (−q⁻¹)ⁿ`, which for odd `n`\ncollapses to `qⁿ − q⁻ⁿ = h·[n]_q`. This proves the arithmetic core of\n`χ_{(2,1)}(σ₁ⁿ)` that does not require the representation itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.habiroLeadingCoeff_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.habiroLeadingCoeff_eq","kind":"theorem","line":420,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L420-L421","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.habiroLeadingCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.habiroLeadingCoeff","kind":"def","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L414-L418","doc":"The leading Habiro coefficient `a₀(A) = 2 × 8^A`. The `8` is the per-nucleon\noctahedron count `borromeanOctahedra`; the `2` is `dim(V_{(2,1)})`, forced by the\nconfinement-SDP interface block (the unique Wedderburn block carrying both\neigenvalues `+q` and `-q⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.borromeanOctahedra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.borromeanOctahedra","kind":"def","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L410-L412","doc":"The number of ideal octahedra in the Borromean complement\n(`Vol(𝓑₃) = 8G`, `G` = Catalan's constant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.deltaLambda_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.deltaLambda_eq","kind":"theorem","line":398,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L398-L404","doc":"`Δ_λ` expressed via the conjugate-parabolic sign × dimension (proved modulo the\nsign-rule formalisation target `sign_rule_conjugate_parabolic`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.deltaLambda","kind":"def","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L392-L396","doc":"The per-partition binding weight `Δ_λ = sgn(w_0^{S_{λ'}}) × f^λ` — the\nconjugate-parabolic sign times the regular-representation multiplicity. Both\nfactors are categorical (independent of the deformation parameter `q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_5","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L376-L386","doc":"Burnside `Σ (f^λ)² = 5! = 120` at `n = 5` (`f = 1, 4, 5, 6, 5, 4, 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_4","kind":"theorem","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L366-L374","doc":"Burnside `Σ (f^λ)² = 4! = 24` at `n = 4` (`f = 1, 3, 2, 3, 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_3","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L359-L364","doc":"Burnside `Σ (f^λ)² = 3! = 6` at `n = 3` (`f = 1, 2, 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_2","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L353-L357","doc":"Burnside `Σ (f^λ)² = 2! = 2` at `n = 2` (`f = 1, 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside_check_1","kind":"theorem","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L348-L351","doc":"Burnside `Σ (f^λ)² = 1! = 1` at `n = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.burnside","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L302-L338","doc":"Burnside / RSK: `Σ_λ (f^λ)² = n!` over the *complete, deduplicated* set of\npartitions of `n`. The regular representation decomposes as `⊕_λ f^λ · V_λ`, so\n`dim(reg) = Σ (f^λ)² = n!`. This is exactly axiom (i) of the Identity-I program;\nfaithfully stated with completeness + no-duplication hypotheses on `partitions`\n(via `Partition.parts`, which carries `DecidableEq`). Formalisation target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.BurnsideContext.burnside_claim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.BurnsideContext.burnside_claim","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L297-L297","doc":"The burnside claim (conclusion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.BurnsideContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.BurnsideContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L295-L295","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.BurnsideContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.BurnsideContext","kind":"class","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L295-L300","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.sign_rule_conjugate_parabolic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.sign_rule_conjugate_parabolic","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L281-L289","doc":"Corollary `(-1)^{n(λ)} = Π_j (-1)^{C(λ'_j,2)} = Π_j sgn(w_0^{S_{λ'_j}})` — the\nsign of the longest element of the conjugate parabolic `S_{λ'} ⊂ S_n`. The sign-\nmultiplicativity step (`neg_one_pow_list_sum`) and the Macdonald identity\n`nStat_eq_sum_choose2_conjugate` it rests on are now both proved, so this corollary is\nfully sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.nStat_eq_sum_choose2_conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.nStat_eq_sum_choose2_conjugate","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L246-L271","doc":"The Macdonald identity `n(λ) = Σ_j C(λ'_j, 2)`: `n(λ) = Σ_i i·λ_i` counts each\ncell `(i,j)` by its row index `i`; grouping by column `j`, column `j` has `λ'_j`\ncells in rows `0,…,λ'_j-1`, contributing `Σ_{i<λ'_j} i = C(λ'_j, 2)`.\nProved sorry-free via the row/column peel `rowStat_eq_colStat` (the Fubini swap over\ndiagram cells; both sides satisfy the same column-peeling recursion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.rowStat_eq_colStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.rowStat_eq_colStat","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L224-L238","doc":"For a weakly-decreasing list bounded by `M`, the row statistic equals the column\nstatistic: `rowStat L = colStat L M`. The Fubini swap over Young-diagram cells, proved by\npeeling the largest row (`rowStat_cons`) against the column peel (`colStat_cons`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Ssum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Ssum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L198-L222","doc":"The double-count remainder equals `l.sum` when `a` dominates `l` and `a ≤ M`:\n`Σ_{j<M} (if j<a then #{x∈l : x>j} else 0) = Σ_{x∈l} x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.colStat_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.colStat_cons","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L179-L196","doc":"`colStat` peels column-0, leaving an explicit double-count remainder (no sortedness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.rowStat_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.rowStat_cons","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L164-L177","doc":"`rowStat` peels the index-0 (largest) row: `rowStat (a :: l) = rowStat l + l.sum`. The\nremaining rows drop their index by one, reducing `n(λ)` by `Σ l = l.sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.indicator_lt_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.indicator_lt_sum","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L154-L162","doc":"Indicator count: `Σ_{j<M} [j<b] = min b M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_succ","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L148-L152","doc":"Pascal step for `choose2`: `C(c+1, 2) = C(c, 2) + c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.colStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.colStat","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L143-L146","doc":"Column statistic with explicit column bound `M`: `Σ_{j<M} C(#{x∈L : x>j}, 2)`. For\n`M = λ_1` (the largest part) this is `(conjugate.map choose2).sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.rowStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.rowStat","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L140-L141","doc":"Row statistic on a raw list: `Σ_i i·L[i]` via `zipIdx`; `Λ.nStat = rowStat Λ.parts`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.dimIrrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.dimIrrep","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L127-L131","doc":"`f^λ = n! / (hook product)` — the number of standard Young tableaux, i.e. the\ndimension of the irreducible `S_n`-representation `V_λ` (and its multiplicity in\nthe regular representation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.hookProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.hookProduct","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L121-L125","doc":"Product of all hook lengths in a partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.hookLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.hookLength","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L117-L119","doc":"Hook length at cell `(i,j)` = arm + leg + 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.legLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.legLength","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L113-L115","doc":"Leg length at cell `(i,j)`: number of cells below in column `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.armLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.armLength","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L107-L111","doc":"Arm length at cell `(i,j)`: number of cells to the right in row `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.sgnLongest_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.sgnLongest_one","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.sgnLongest_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.sgnLongest_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.sgnLongest","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.sgnLongest","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L97-L98","doc":"The sign of the longest element of `S_k` is `(-1)^{k(k-1)/2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_three","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_two","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_one","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2_zero","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.choose2","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L89-L90","doc":"`C(k, 2) = k(k-1)/2` — the length of the longest element of `S_k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.conjugate","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L83-L87","doc":"Conjugate partition `λ'` — the `j`-th part counts cells in column `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.nStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.nStat","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L76-L81","doc":"`n(λ) = Σ_i i × λ_i` — the weighted sum of parts (0-indexed); equivalently the\nsum of row indices of all cells in the Young diagram. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.length","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L73-L74","doc":"Number of parts (length of the partition). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.empty","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L66-L71","doc":"The empty partition of 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.ext_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.ext_iff","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.ext","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L52-L64","doc":"**Extensionality.** `parts` is the only data field — `pos`, `sum_eq` and `sorted`\nare `Prop`s — so two partitions of `n` agree as soon as their part lists do.\n\n`QOU.BraidKnot.PartitionNatBridge` has always called this as `Partition.ext'`, but\nno such declaration existed anywhere in the file's history: `Partition` carries no\n`@[ext]` attribute, so nothing generated one. That call site could never have\nelaborated; it went unnoticed only because this module already failed to compile\n(the LWC-2 namespace sweep, repaired in the preceding commit), so nothing\ndownstream was ever reached. Declared here under the idiomatic `@[ext]` name, with\nthe call site updated to match. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.sorted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.sorted","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.pos","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.parts","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DeltaLambdaSignRule.Partition","kind":"structure","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DeltaLambdaSignRule.lean#L45-L50","doc":"A partition of `n` as a weakly decreasing list of positive naturals. ","signatureChunk":0}]}